e_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/53","text":"forms in approximately equal proportions. A band migrating at lower molecular weight than FO was observed for the mutant FcA_103-117. Although the identity of this band has not been thoroughly investigated, it may represent the FO precursor of the FcA_103-117 mutant, which lacks an N-glycosylation site that has previously been shown to be used in the Z strain of SeV F protein (N104) (35)."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"When trypsin was added to the medium of the transfected cells (Fig: 3B, lower panel), cleavage of the FO precursor of both Fsev and F_RKR to Fl was clearly enhanced In contrast, only a slight increase in FO processing was detected when  trypsin was  added to cells   expressing the Fc mutant. However; the extent of FO-to-Fl cleavage was enhanced by trypsin in all four Fsev mutants containing both FRsv cleavage sites; and Fc_103-130 appeared  fully cleaved to Fl in the presence of trypsin: Thus, insertion of an FRsv cleavage site II in the SeV F protein increases the extent of cleavage at this site in the absence of trypsin. This cleavage is further enhanced by wild-type","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":54.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":41.666666666666664,"r":285.0,"t":77.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,117],"page_no":1},{"bbox":{"b":53.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":299.3333333333333,"r":543.0,"t":156.62869378504422},"charspan":[118,677],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/54","text":"When trypsin was added to the medium of the transfected cells (Fig: 3B, lower panel), cleavage of the FO precursor of both Fsev and F_RKR to Fl was clearly enhanced In contrast, only a slight increase in FO processing was detected when  trypsin was  added to cells   expressing the Fc mutant. However; the extent of FO-to-Fl cleavage was enhanced by trypsin in all four Fsev mutants containing both FRsv cleavage sites; and Fc_103-130 appeared  fully cleaved to Fl in the presence of trypsin: Thus, insertion of an FRsv cleavage site II in the SeV F protein increases the extent of cleavage at this site in the absence of trypsin. This cleavage is further enhanced by wild-type"}],"version":"1.10.0"}